# tools/update-trial's first run: the device as made - release 1 in
# slot A, rollback index 3, trust list v1 - boots slot A and takes the bundle
# of release 2: trust list v2 first, then the whole image into slot B,
# checked against the manifest and marked for one trial, security version 5.
# The harness checks the SHA-256 the stand-in reports for slot B is release
# 2's image's.
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children update_storage (0), update (1) and update_bundles (2)
NOWAYOS: update-bundles: starting
NOWAYOS: update-bundles: this image is release 1
NOWAYOS: update-bundles: the disk handed to the storage stand-in: 1736 bytes
NOWAYOS: update-bundles: 1 bundles from fw_cfg's opt/nowayos/bundles
NOWAYOS: update-bundles: offering bundle 1 of 1
NOWAYOS: update-storage: starting
NOWAYOS: update-storage: the disk the last run left: booted slot A
NOWAYOS: update-storage: copy A on the disk: generation 1: slot A boots; nothing marked; rollback index 3; trust list v1
NOWAYOS: update-storage: copy B on the disk: empty
NOWAYOS: update: starting
NOWAYOS: update: starting: slot A boots; trial: none; rollback index 3; trust list v1 (held, checked against the anchors)
NOWAYOS: update: slot A runs, from the slot marked good; 1 trust anchor(s) in the image
NOWAYOS: update-storage: copy B written: generation 2: slot A boots; nothing marked; rollback index 3; trust list v2
NOWAYOS: update-storage: copy A written: generation 3: slot A boots; slot B marked for one trial, security version 5; rollback index 3; trust list v2
NOWAYOS: update: bundle 1: staged in slot B for one trial; restart wanted
NOWAYOS: update-bundles: all 1 bundles offered

# Output that fails the run at once if it appears anywhere.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!not taken
!: does not decode
!refused
